        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "05bb9a35-61c4-3a45-ac61-b951bbb92b30",
                "word": "pétrel",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "4ab37a4d-890e-43e2-9d84-2473d8e701c2",
                        "entry_id": "05bb9a35-61c4-3a45-ac61-b951bbb92b30",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "pétrels"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "68445d2e-1d97-32db-97d8-97a73c32968a",
                        "entry_id": "05bb9a35-61c4-3a45-ac61-b951bbb92b30",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Oiseau nageur de haute mer, au vol bas et rapide, dont la présence passe pour annoncer aux navigateurs l’approche des tempêtes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "aafb2d8c-54ba-4c0b-8865-da8061c1c73e",
                                "sense_id": "68445d2e-1d97-32db-97d8-97a73c32968a",
                                "text": "La preuve en est dans le fait, constaté bien des fois, que par vent modéré, les pétrels faisaient imperturbablement leurs manœuvres sans aucun mouvement des ailes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "57b459b9-5232-41aa-af3e-dd3928c1208c",
                                "sense_id": "68445d2e-1d97-32db-97d8-97a73c32968a",
                                "text": "Nous observâmes une quantité de petits pétrels volant en tout sens autour du navire, mais principalement au-dessus et dans l’ouaiche, lesquels je reconnus pour le Procellaria oceanica."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d1cdb2d-3a05-4ca9-9496-ed6cfae74369",
                                "sense_id": "68445d2e-1d97-32db-97d8-97a73c32968a",
                                "text": "Quelques oiseaux retardataires, des pétrels, des guillemots, des puffins, animaient encore cette solitude et jetaient des cris perçants."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e1c621d2-eb3f-4191-8792-01d890d85d76",
                                "sense_id": "68445d2e-1d97-32db-97d8-97a73c32968a",
                                "text": "Le pétrel des Bermudes, l’oiseau emblématique de cet archipel britannique situé dans l’océan Atlantique, a été redécouvert en 1951, près de 300 ans après sa prétendue extinction."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3954444f-21dc-4c5f-a055-ea20c1ca4cab",
                                "sense_id": "68445d2e-1d97-32db-97d8-97a73c32968a",
                                "text": "… on rencontrait des familles d’albatros, de malamochs, de pétrels gris, de damiers blancs et noirs, qui flottaient à la dérive ; ils étaient posés et ils dormaient."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5e3bb00f-b91b-4130-8e56-a48f46341965",
                        "source_entry_id": "05bb9a35-61c4-3a45-ac61-b951bbb92b30",
                        "source_sense_id": "68445d2e-1d97-32db-97d8-97a73c32968a",
                        "target_lang_word": "petrel",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "petrel",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0758704d-e814-3139-b536-f2fea181afbb",
                                        "entry_id": "e5e40532-e250-3132-ac0e-46177124071b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of various species of black, grey, or white seabirds in the order Procellariiformes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15bd44ba-9f43-4717-8064-782b6a7829fa",
                                                "sense_id": "0758704d-e814-3139-b536-f2fea181afbb",
                                                "text": "The seventh of May following, we first saw many Birds in bignesse of Cliffe Pidgeons, and after divers other as Pettrels, Cootes, Hagbuts, Pengwins, Murres, Gannets, Cormorants, Guls, with many else in our English Tongue of no name."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83479d35-529e-410d-b23d-ef719454f65c",
                                                "sense_id": "0758704d-e814-3139-b536-f2fea181afbb",
                                                "text": "In a storm they will hover close under the ship's stern in the wake of the ship (as it is called) or the smoothness which the ship's passing has made on the sea; and there as they fly (gently then) they pat the water alternately with their feet as if they walked upon it; though still upon the wing. And from hence the seamen give them the name of petrels in allusion to St. Peter's walking upon the Lake of Gennesareth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
